# Git deploy workflow (bchata)

When you finish implementing or fixing code in this repo:

1. Run `npm run build` and fix failures until it succeeds.
2. Commit only the files changed for the task (never commit secrets).
3. Run `git push origin main` immediately — do not ask the user to confirm push.

Report briefly when done: build result, commit hash/message, and that push completed. No "should I push?" prompts.

Only skip push if the user explicitly says not to push in that message, or if commit is impossible (nothing to commit).
